<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24801" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαθήκη</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διατίθημι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>disposition</i> of property by will, <i>testament,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				584
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				589
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				27.13
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ διαθήκην</span> by
				<i>will</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				753.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cilicia</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Test.Epict.</u>
				4.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1113.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>, etc.: in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαθήκας διαθέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					19.39
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CIG</u>
					2690
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Iasus</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἀπόρρητοι δ.</span> mystic
				<i>deposits</i> on which the common weal depended, prob.
			oracles  (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαθέτης</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Din.
				1.9
			</span></i> codd. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> name of
			an eyesalve, because the recipe was <i>deposited</i> in a temple,
				<i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				7.118
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>compact, covenant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢν μὴ διαθῶνται διαθήκην ἐμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					440
				</span></i>
			; freq. in <i><span class="en">LXX, <u>Ge.</u>
				6.18</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καινή, παλαιὰ δ.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				22.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Cor.</u>
				3.14
			</span></i>; <i>disposition</i> (with allusion to <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Gal.</u>
				3.15
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
				9.15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάθεσις</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σώματος δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
